{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trace-governed excess on this trip is 5.0 km over the booked optimal of 19.6 km, or 25.51%. That clears POL-RD-01's establishment gate (more than 20% and more than 0.8 km) but falls a long way short of its materiality gate of more than 50% of optimal or more than 8.0 km absolute. No MATERIAL deviation is recorded, so the material-deviation regime in POL-RD-06 — the only route to a FULL refund on rider-side evidence — is not engaged, and the driver's liability is bounded by the ordinary POL-RD-02 recomputation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00508", "EV-TRIP-00508"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The whole of the driver's monetary exposure is fixed by POL-RD-02's arithmetic, run on the fare_breakdown itself: recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 19.6 km + 0.28 x 26.0 min) x 1.0 surge + 0.80 platform fee = 26.58, against a charged_total of 32.57, giving a refund of 5.99 rounded up to SGD 6.00. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 and not POL-RD-11 supplies the remedy, and the rider's claim to the full SGD 32.57 she has contested is unsupported on the platform's own arithmetic.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00508", "EV-TRIP-00508"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The computed refund is 18.4% of charged_total, nowhere near the 90% share POL-RD-02 requires before FULL_REFUND displaces the partial, and it is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis so it does not collapse to no action either. The only outcome the arithmetic supports is a bounded PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 6.00 — not the complete reversal the rider seeks.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00508"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_share_of_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Every dollar on the receipt is meter arithmetic on the route actually driven: 3.80 base fare, 18.45 distance (24.6 km x 0.75), 9.52 time (34.0 min x 0.28) and 0.80 platform fee, with surge_multiplier 1.0 read from the fare_breakdown, zero ERP lines, no airport surcharge, no waiting fee and no promo. There is no unmatched or phantom charge line, no billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09, and nothing on the receipt sustains the rider's 'ripping people off' characterisation beyond the 5.0 km of established excess itself.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00508"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Any repeat-deviation uplift is foreclosed on the driver's own record: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 250, so no pattern is ESTABLISHED under POL-RD-06 and neither the deterrent FULL_REFUND uplift in limb (b) nor the conduct referral in limb (c) can attach. POL-GEN-01 confines that profile to that named test, and no other field on it may carry any finding against the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00508"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's explanation of a CTE queue at the Braddell exit is tested against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else. EV-ADVIS-00508-01 is MISSING — issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0, no payload and no validity window — so POL-RD-03 cannot be run on the record and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. The driver cited no advisory identifier, so the absence is a gap in the bundle and not a clause invoked against a cited artifact; under POL-RD-13 that gap does not engage POL-RD-10(5). The consequence is a ruling on the measured excess with the ordinary POL-RD-02 refund, not an escalation and not an enlargement of the excess.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00508-01", "EV-TRIP-00508"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account — 'same route every time, never above 40' and a referral to the authorities — is narrative with no artifact behind it: the trip's chat log is empty (message_count 0) and no admissible document records any usual-price benchmark. POL-RD-02 makes the refund arithmetic rather than discretionary and POL-RD-08 gives no weight to assertions that cite no evidence ID, so this trip is priced from its own trace and its own booked optimal, and nothing entitles the rider to more than the SGD 6.00 that arithmetic produces.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00508", "EV-TRIP-00508", "EV-FARE-00508"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

