    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 6.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "This ruling is for both parties. The dispute is over a Woodlands MRT to Novena Square taxi trip on 27 Aug 2026, charged at SGD 32.57 (EV-FARE-00508).\n\nTo the rider: your route-deviation claim is made out, though not for the amount you contested. The governing measurement under POL-RD-01 is the GPS trace, not the trip record's rounded copy. The trace shows 24.6 km driven against a booked optimal of 19.6 km (EV-GPS-00508 and EV-TRIP-00508): an excess of 5.0 km, or 25.51%. Both establishment tests pass — more than 20% of optimal and more than 0.8 km — so a deviation is established. It does not reach the materiality gate of more than 50% or more than 8.0 km, so the repeat-deviation regime in POL-RD-06 is not engaged, and the driver's profile in any event shows deviation_flags_90d of 0 against 250 completed trips in 90 days. Your claim to the whole SGD 32.57 is not supported: the fare is METERED, so POL-RD-02 fixes the remedy arithmetically. Recomputing on the booked optimal route: (base fare 3.80 + 0.75 x 19.6 km + 0.28 x 26.0 min) x surge 1.0 (read from the fare_breakdown, EV-FARE-00508) + 0.80 platform fee = a recomputed fare of 26.58. Refund = charged_total 32.57 - 26.58 = 5.99, which is above the 0.50 de minimis and well below the 90% share that would trigger a full refund (it is 18.39% of the charge). Rounded up, you are refunded SGD 6.00. Your 'same route every time, never above 40' benchmark is not evidence of this trip's correct fare — the chat log for this trip is empty (0 messages) and no admissible artifact records a usual-price benchmark — so the trip is priced from its own trace and its own booked optimal.\n\nTo the driver: your explanation that you took the BKE-PIE route because of a CTE queue at the Braddell exit carries no weight. An external-traffic excuse is tested against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else (POL-RD-13, POL-RD-03). The only advisory artifact in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-00508-01, is MISSING, with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight_multiplier 0.0 and no payload, so it can carry no fact and POL-RD-03 cannot be run. Because you cited no advisory identifier, that absence is a gap in the bundle rather than a clause invoked against a cited artifact, so it does not trigger escalation under POL-RD-10(5). The deviation therefore stands at the measured 5.0 km and no amended optimal is substituted. Your point that the rider's usual price depends on time of day does not assist: the recomputation runs on this trip's own stored rate card and a surge multiplier of 1.0 from the fare_breakdown.\n\nThe trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a)-(c): coverage is 100%, there are no gaps, max gap is 0.0 s, and the sampling interval is 10 s across 205 fixes, so the deviation rests on an unimpaired trace and needs no corroboration beyond it.\n\nNo other exculpatory route applies: there is no rider-requested detour (the chat log is empty, POL-RD-04), no amended pickup or dropoff (both amendment timestamps and both amended-optimal fields are null, POL-RD-05), and the vehicle is RYDE_TAXI, not a pooled trip (POL-RD-12). On the receipt (EV-FARE-00508) every line is meter arithmetic on the driven route with zero ERP, no airport surcharge and no waiting fee, so there is no billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4) and no referral arises. No clause in this case produces a referral: the POL-RD-06 pattern test fails, there is no phantom charge line under POL-RD-09(4), and no false-arrival or no-show clause is in play. The confidence of 0.9 is within the cap set by the deciding artifacts, all of which carry weight 1.0. The platform-wide escalation floor of 0.70 is not reached. outcome: a partial refund of SGD 6.00 to the rider; the balance of the SGD 32.57 charge stands."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

