    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim that this trip was driven further than it should have been is made out, but it is worth SGD 6.00, not the SGD 32.57 you contested. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00508 records 24.6 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff; the booked optimal distance on EV-TRIP-00508 is 19.6 km. That is an excess of 5.0 km, or 25.51% of optimal, measured on the trace figure as POL-RD-01 requires (the trip record's 24.6 km is a rounded copy of the same measurement and is not the field used for the threshold test). Both limbs of POL-RD-01's establishment gate pass: more than 20% and more than 0.8 km. The excess does not reach materiality (which needs more than 50% or more than 8.0 km), so the repeat-deviation regime in POL-RD-06 is not engaged and no uplift applies. The fare is METERED, so POL-RD-02 supplies the remedy and not POL-RD-11. Recomputing on the optimal route: (3.80 base + 0.75 x 19.6 km + 0.28 x 26.0 min) x surge 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee = 26.58. The surge multiplier of 1.0 is read from EV-FARE-00508 itself. Refund = charged_total 32.57 - recomputed_fare 26.58 = 5.99, rounded up to SGD 6.00. That is 18.39% of the charge, well below the 90% share that would make it a full refund, and above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor, so it is a partial refund. Nothing on the receipt is a phantom charge: the ledger shows zero ERP lines, no airport surcharge, no waiting fee and no promo, and the billed distance matches the trace, so there is no separate billing-integrity correction and no POL-RD-09(4) referral. Your statements that the same route never costs above 40 and that you have reported the matter to the authorities are narrative: the chat log for this trip (EV-CHAT-00508) is empty and no admissible artifact records a usual-price benchmark or any other fare, so they cannot move the arithmetic and the fare is recomputed from this trip's own rate card. To the driver: your explanation of a CTE queue at the Braddell exit does not assist you. The only advisory artifact in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-00508-01, is MISSING - issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0, no payload - so it can carry no fact and POL-RD-03 cannot be run: there is no advisory naming a road the optimal route traverses with a validity window overlapping the time the trace shows the vehicle reaching that segment. Under POL-RD-13 the assertion is tested against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else, and it carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Because you named no advisory identifier, this is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) does not fire and the case is decided on the measured excess with the ordinary POL-RD-02 refund; the excess is neither reduced nor enlarged. Your point that the rider's usual price depends on time of day is correct as a general matter but does not change this trip: the stored surge multiplier on this trip's fare_breakdown is 1.0. On the driver's record, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 250, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established and neither the deterrent full-refund uplift nor the driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06 attaches (POL-GEN-01 confines that artifact to that named test). For both parties, the trace is not impaired for policy purposes: EV-GPS-00508 has 100% coverage, an empty gap array, a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds and a 10 second sampling interval across 205 fixes, so none of POL-RD-07's limbs fires and no independent corroboration is needed. EV-TRIP-00508 and EV-FARE-00508 both carry trip TRP-00508 and the trace's first fix matches the recorded start, so the rider's burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged and no exculpatory clause (POL-RD-03, POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-12) applies: the chat log is empty, no amendment timestamp or amended optimal exists, and the vehicle type is RYDE_TAXI, not RYDE_POOL. No unbilled-distance compensation is due to the driver: the ledger's charged distance of 24.6 km equals the trace distance, so there is no shortfall over 1.0 km under POL-RD-04. The disputed amount beyond the SGD 6.00 refund stands, and no referral or escalation is required."
